# Per-project `to-do.md` (required)

## Rule

- Each **first-class program / app** living under **`Programs/`** (e.g. `Programs/<area>/<project-name>/`) **must** include a **`to-do.md`** at that project root.
- **New project:** Create **`to-do.md`** in the same commit or PR that introduces the project folder (or immediately after), before the work is considered “handed off.”
- **Scope:** One file per project — do **not** use a single global to-do for unrelated programs.

## What to put in `to-do.md`

- **Short overview** of the project’s purpose (1–3 sentences).
- **Integrations / risky work** (e.g. payments, auth, third-party APIs) with a realistic difficulty note and bullet checklist.
- **Backlog** — actionable items.
- **Done / archived** — optional; move finished items here with a brief note.

## Example (this repo)

- **`Programs/Pickleball/advanced-open-play/to-do.md`** — Open Play Firebase app (RSVP, account, check-in); includes Stripe assessment and backlog.

## Agent behavior

- When **adding** a new folder under **`Programs/`** that is a deployable or maintainable “project,” **create `to-do.md`** there using the structure above unless the user explicitly defers it (then still mention it as follow-up).
- When **planning** large features (payments, new hosting, rules changes), **update** that project’s **`to-do.md`** so the backlog stays the single place for roadmap items.
